WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
Letting AI write code is easier than ever.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:03.740
But what did it change?

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.190
And if it takes a wrong turn,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.560
how do you step back?

00:00:07.155 --> 00:00:07.975
DeltaBox Lite:

00:00:08.535 --> 00:00:10.665
keep changes easy to inspect and keep,

00:00:11.195 --> 00:00:12.155
while safe to undo.

00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:14.585
It starts with a simple file modification.

00:00:15.045 --> 00:00:17.915
DeltaBox introduces Commit-Biased Copy-on-Write.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.600
Commit-Biased Copy-on-Write updates the workspace in place,

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.990
while capturing a safe baseline for potential rollbacks.

00:00:24.602 --> 00:00:25.972
Before any data is overwritten,

00:00:26.342 --> 00:00:29.542
the system first records the original range into an undo log.

00:00:30.205 --> 00:00:32.705
New data is then written directly to the workspace.

00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:34.705
Changes are live immediately,

00:00:35.295 --> 00:00:36.765
completely transparent to your tools.

00:00:37.465 --> 00:00:38.975
If you are happy with the result,

00:00:39.015 --> 00:00:41.445
commit seals the current state, keeping the changes.

00:00:42.122 --> 00:00:43.192
If you need to roll back,

00:00:43.232 --> 00:00:44.392
abort replays the log,

00:00:44.492 --> 00:00:47.042
instantly restoring the workspace to how it was before.

00:00:47.695 --> 00:00:50.545
In-place writes preserve seamless developer workflows.

00:00:51.185 --> 00:00:52.995
The undo log protects your baseline.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.293
Integrated with DeepSeek Harness.

00:00:56.063 --> 00:00:57.063
When files are modified,

00:00:57.553 --> 00:00:59.433
a review panel outlines the changes.

00:01:00.123 --> 00:01:00.713
Reject it,

00:01:01.263 --> 00:01:02.773
and the modifications are rolled back.

00:01:04.445 --> 00:01:07.315
If you approve the changes, select "Allow once".

00:01:08.015 --> 00:01:11.155
DeltaBox commits the state, and the agent moves on to the next task.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:12.700
Inside Pi,

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.900
run sandbox review to inspect the diff.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:19.955
Once verified,

00:01:20.305 --> 00:01:22.375
run sandbox commit to keep the result.

00:01:28.425 --> 00:01:29.895
Want to discard the next attempt?

00:01:30.505 --> 00:01:31.855
Just type sandbox abort.

00:01:33.955 --> 00:01:34.745
Confirm with Enter,

00:01:35.215 --> 00:01:38.295
and the workspace reverts to the clean state before this run.

00:01:39.872 --> 00:01:41.552
Two distinct agent workflows,

00:01:41.872 --> 00:01:43.942
powered by the exact same state engine.

00:01:44.702 --> 00:01:46.942
Native on Linux and macOS.

00:01:47.622 --> 00:01:48.582
Let agents explore.

00:01:49.112 --> 00:01:50.462
Keep the choice in your hands.

00:01:51.212 --> 00:01:52.012
DeltaBox Lite,

00:01:52.602 --> 00:01:54.192
giving every attempt a choice.
